From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Stockdale <jstockdale@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:40:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Input: nt36536: give the touch and pen devices an identity
 and the pen its parent

Ours (2026-11-03, A.3c N6). Exit: offer upstream with the series.

Both input devices registered with vendor and product 0, and the pen
device had no parent, so it lived under /devices/virtual. libwacom, and
with it GNOME's Graphics Tablets panel, identifies a tablet by bus,
vendor and product and found nothing to match ("is a tablet but not
supported by libwacom"). Report Novatek's vendor id and the controller
as the product on both devices, and hang the pen device off the SPI
controller it belongs to.

Signed-off-by: John Stockdale <jstockdale@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c
index 28a8e70c86bb..a7af60c9822e 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c
@@ -67,6 +67,10 @@ static uint8_t bTouchIsAwake = 0;
 #define NVT_EXT_PEN_OFF		0x11
 #define NVT_PEN_UPLINK_RESUME	1
 
+/* input device identity: Novatek Microelectronics' vendor id, the controller as the product */
+#define NVT_ID_VENDOR		0x0603
+#define NVT_ID_PRODUCT		0x6536
+
 static unsigned int pen_type = 1;
 
 /*
@@ -1718,6 +1722,9 @@ static int32_t nvt_ts_probe(struct spi_device *client)
 	ts->input_dev->name = NVT_TS_NAME;
 	ts->input_dev->phys = ts->phys;
 	ts->input_dev->id.bustype = BUS_SPI;
+	/* Novatek's vendor id and the controller, so userspace (libwacom) can tell the devices apart */
+	ts->input_dev->id.vendor = NVT_ID_VENDOR;
+	ts->input_dev->id.product = NVT_ID_PRODUCT;
 
 	//---register input device---
 	ret = input_register_device(ts->input_dev);
@@ -1767,6 +1774,10 @@ static int32_t nvt_ts_probe(struct spi_device *client)
 		ts->pen_input_dev->name = NVT_PEN_NAME;
 		ts->pen_input_dev->phys = ts->pen_phys;
 		ts->pen_input_dev->id.bustype = BUS_SPI;
+		ts->pen_input_dev->id.vendor = NVT_ID_VENDOR;
+		ts->pen_input_dev->id.product = NVT_ID_PRODUCT;
+		/* the pen belongs to the controller, not to the virtual tree */
+		ts->pen_input_dev->dev.parent = &client->dev;
 
 		//---register pen input device---
 		ret = input_register_device(ts->pen_input_dev);
-- 
